Changelog: 21-10-2026 02:13:00

Release 0.7.1.

Changelog: 21-10-2026 01:54:13

Breaking. The app is BC-250 Upscaler Manager (owner, 21-10-2026: it is not HelixSR itself, and the old name
confused people), in the window, the menu entry, the portal and the wiki. With the name go the folder apps/upscaler,
the package upscaler, the portal key upscaler, the release tags upscaler-v<x.y.z>, the wiki chapter
docs/apps/upscaler.md and the installed name bc250-upscaler: the launcher ~/.local/bin/bc250-upscaler, the folders
~/.local/share/bc250-upscaler and ~/.config/bc250-upscaler, the desktop entry and the icon. install.sh takes over a
copy installed as bc250-bazzite-helixsr-gui, on install and uninstall: the imported payload, the settings
(bc250-bazzite-helixsr-gui.conf becomes bc250-upscaler.conf) and the list of deployed games move to the new folders
(not over ones that are there already), the old launcher, menu entry, Desktop icon, icons and the rest of the old
folder (venv, downloads) go. The games themselves are not touched. HelixSR keeps its name wherever the app means the
upscaler it deploys. The portal notice of a newer HelixSR is published under the key upscaler. The installer test
plants a copy under the old name.

Changelog: 21-10-2026 01:43:59

Added. With OptiScaler installed for a Steam game (Deploy, stand-alone folder), the app also sets the game's Steam
launch options (owner, 21-10-2026): WINEDLLOVERRIDES="dxgi=n,b" (under the name OptiScaler got), added to the
launch options already there, for every Steam user (userdata/<user>/config/localconfig.vdf, only that line changes).
Steam writes that file again when it closes, so the app asks to close it, sets them and starts Steam again
(bc250_core.steam.with_steam_closed, as Console Link does); in Game Mode Steam stays open and the line is copied to the
clipboard. OptiScaler's record in the HelixSR folder keeps the launch options of before, and Remove puts them back
unless they were changed since. helixsr now uses bc250_core (its steam module only, owner, 21-10-2026): install.sh
copies it from the checkout as a release bundles it, and uninstalls it. Help, the Deploy page and the wiki say so.
Tests: tests/test_optiscaler.py (reading and writing localconfig.vdf, adding the override, the record) and
tests/test_main_window.py (Deploy and Remove with Steam running, Game Mode); the installer test checks the core.

