DLSS DLL) is tried again, 3 seconds apart, five times in all; then the setup says "Server currently not available.
Try again later." Cancel works during the pause. Other answers fail at once, as before.

Changelog: 20-10-2026 21:58:19

Release 0.7.0.

Changelog: 20-10-2026 21:34:32

Added. HelixSR 2.x is set up (owner, 20-10-2026). Its helixsr-setup.sh hands --yes on to its game installer, which
would put HelixSR Scaler into every game it finds, and its license does not allow changing the script; so for 2.x the
app runs what the script runs before its games: HelixSR's own builder, unchanged (setup/helixsr_setup.py on the
release's HelixSR-fsrfg folder, --yes --no-fg, the DLSS DLL with --dlss), with the portable Python (numpy installed by
pip when it has none, as the script does) or the system's python3 with numpy, the shader compiler through the Wine
the script would use (Steam's Proton first) and a wrapper of the app's own in its work folder; Wine's temporary prefix
is removed afterwards, and the build counts only when --status says network=1. The DLL is taken from HelixSR-fsrfg
(payload_folder in backend.py); 1.x still runs its setup script. SUPPORTED_MAJOR is 2 (1.x stays available) and
KNOWN_VERSION 2.0.0; the Setup page, the help and the wiki say so. The downloaded DLSS DLL is now also deleted when the
build stops with an error. Tests: tests/test_acquire.py (a fake 2.x release whose setup script must not run, a fake
builder, the DXC wrapper's paths, Wine and Python choice).

