Changelog: 19-10-2026 21:45:21

Release 0.5.0.

Changelog: 19-10-2026 20:53:49

Added. A Games page: every Steam game on this PC (Steam's own Proton, runtime and redistributable folders left out),
each looked through in the background for an AMD FSR 3.1 DLL; the games that have one come first with HelixSR's
state (not installed, installed, an older build, or the game's own DLL back), the others are grayed out and Open on
Deploy page takes them to OptiScaler. Run with HelixSR (or a double-click) puts HelixSR in where it is missing,
older or replaced by the game's own DLL, keeping the game's helixsr.ini and backup, then starts the game through
Steam (steam://rungameid/<AppID>, the AppID from the library's appmanifest); it asks before the first install into a
game and changes nothing while the game runs (Steam's AppId=<id> on a running process). Update older games on the
Overview puts the payload's HelixSR into every deployment with an older build or the game's own DLL back, keeping
helixsr.ini, a stand-alone folder's second upscaler and the game's backup; after a build the app offers it. Download
and build does not start with less than about 1.5 GB free.

Changelog: 19-10-2026 20:53:49

