showed Older build on the Overview, and Deploy listed its DLL as HelixSR of another build; it is Original restored,
as the help says, and Game's own DLL again. A DLL is HelixSR when it is the payload's, carries the network, or names
its HelixSR version (1.4.3 and newer do).

Changelog: 19-10-2026 20:28:50

Fixed. HelixSR 2.0.0 is not set up: its helixsr-setup.sh hands --yes on to its game installer, which then puts
HelixSR Scaler with frame generation into every game it finds, and its package keeps the DLL in HelixSR-fsrfg/. The
app sets up HelixSR 1.x only (SUPPORTED_MAJOR in acquire.py): the update check reads GitHub's list of releases and
takes the newest stable 1.x release with its HelixSR-x.y.z.zip (1.9.3), and the Setup page and the Overview say when
a newer major version is out that the app does not support yet. The portal's notice offers only what Get HelixSR…
installs. Download and build refuses a release of another major version. The release zip is checked against the
SHA-256 GitHub publishes for it (a cached zip too); a zip that does not match is deleted.

